    <!-- Shown when a session starts; lines kept short for phone screens -->
    <string name="motd">"
Qwen Translate · terminal

At translate's > prompt, type text and press
Enter to translate it. ^D leaves for the shell,
where translate starts it again;
translate --help lists the options, e.g.
  translate --to ja 你好
  translate --image picture.png

In other apps: select text and choose Qwen
Translate, or share text or an image here.

The model downloads on first use (2B, 1.3 GB).
On phones with little memory, use 0.8B (0.5 GB):
  echo 'export QWEN_TRANSLATE_MODEL=fast' >> ~/.mkshrc

Keys: ESC ^C ^D TAB arrows, IMAGE, PASTE; the
last one switches sessions (long press: new shell).

"</string>
    <string name="input_queue_full">Input was not sent: too much pending input. Wait for the command or press Ctrl+C, then paste a smaller portion.</string>
